# Normalize every tracked text file to LF, regardless of a runner's own core.autocrlf default.
# Without this, GitHub's windows-latest images (core.autocrlf=true) check the repo out with CRLF,
# which corrupts fixed sha256 hashes, fixture byte-content, and pointer-block round-trips that
# this project's own tests compare byte-for-byte. Tests that specifically need CRLF content build
# it themselves at runtime; none of it is stored in the repo.
* text=auto eol=lf
